# HITL Guided Manual Audit Playbook

Structure: **Pages × roles matrix, split by executor.** Mixed by design: the agent automates every mechanical check; the human validates only what needs human judgment — UX, UI, flows, and processes as a real user experiences them.

---

## When to run

- Before a major release, when end-to-end flows need human sign-off page by page
- After large refactors that touch many pages (routing, auth, layout)
- Periodically on products with role-based access — role experiences drift silently
- When an automated-only audit is insufficient: a tool can prove the page opens, only a human can say the flow makes sense

---

## Division of labor (non-negotiable)

Default every check to the agent. A check moves to the human ONLY if it genuinely requires human perception — how a flow feels, whether copy makes sense in context, whether the UI looks right. Anything a tool can verify with full reliability MUST be automated; never spend human time on a mechanical check.

| Check | Executor | Tooling | Evidence per check |
|---|---|---|---|
| Page opens — HTTP OK, renders, no blank screen | Agent | chrome-devtools MCP: `navigate_page` + `take_snapshot` | Snapshot excerpt |
| Console clean — no errors/warnings | Agent | chrome-devtools MCP: `list_console_messages` | Message dump (empty = pass) |
| Network clean — no failed requests | Agent | chrome-devtools MCP: `list_network_requests` | Non-2xx/3xx request list |
| Smoke interactions — nav, primary CTA, forms respond | Agent | chrome-devtools MCP: `click` / `fill` / `wait_for` | Post-action snapshot |
| Responsive — 375 / 768 / 1280 / 1920 | Agent | chrome-devtools MCP: `resize_page` + `take_screenshot` | Screenshot per breakpoint |
| a11y basics — contrast, labels, landmarks, alt text | Agent | Lighthouse accessibility category (MCP or CLI) | Score + failing audits |
| Performance snapshot (informational) | Agent | Lighthouse performance category | Score per page |
| Flow completeness — can this role achieve the goal? | Human | Manual walkthrough per role | Verdict + note |
| UX quality — friction, confusion, dead ends | Human | Manual walkthrough | Note per page |
| UI judgment — hierarchy, layout, "looks right" | Human | Eyes on screen | Note per page |
| Copy and tone — wording makes sense for this role | Human | Read as the role would | Note |
| Process correctness — matches the real-world process | Human | Domain knowledge | Verdict per process |

Boundary rules:
- The agent NEVER marks a human row; the human NEVER re-does an agent row.
- An agent pass with no recorded evidence is not a pass.
- If a new check appears mid-audit, classify it agent-first: only human if no tool is 100% reliable for it.

---

## Preparation

1. Enumerate pages in scope × roles that use them. Every pair is a checklist unit.
2. Test credentials for each role.
3. chrome-devtools MCP connected; Lighthouse available.
4. Create `checklist.md` in the run folder from the format below — it is also the resume state.

---

## Per-page × per-role checklist format

The run's `checklist.md` is both the work plan and the cursor. One section per page × role pair; agent rows are filled by the agent with evidence links, human rows only by the human.

```markdown
# Checklist — {{DATE}}-<slug>

Cursor: <page> × <role> | session: N | app version: <commit/tag> | updated: {{DATE}}
Legend: [ ] pending · [x] pass · [F] fail → finding ID · [-] n/a

## /dashboard × admin

Agent (automated, evidence per check):
- [x] opens — clean render (evidence/dashboard-admin-open.md)
- [x] console clean — 0 errors (evidence/dashboard-admin-console.md)
- [x] network clean — 0 failed requests
- [x] smoke — primary CTA responds
- [x] responsive 375/768/1280/1920 (evidence/dashboard-admin-*.png)
- [F] a11y basics — Lighthouse 71, 3 contrast failures → BUG-DASH-1
Human (judgment):
- [x] flow: admin reaches the dashboard goal
- [ ] UX friction
- [ ] UI looks right
- [ ] copy makes sense
```

Failures become findings immediately (row in `00-inventory.md`), marked `[F]` with the ID.

---

## Session protocol (agent-led)

1. **Agent sweep first.** For each pending page × role in cursor order: run all agent checks, store evidence, mark rows, register `[F]` findings. Do not wait for the human between pages.
2. **Human pass second.** Present the human only pages whose agent rows are done — never send a human to a page that fails mechanically. Walk their judgment rows per page; record verdicts and notes verbatim.
3. **Update the cursor** after every page × role pair, not at session end — a killed session loses at most one pair.

---

## Resume / cursor state

Multi-session by design. State lives in `checklist.md`:

- **Cursor line** at the top: last completed `<page> × <role>`, session count, app version, date.
- **Row markers are the ground truth** — resume point is the first `[ ]` row after the cursor; markers win over the cursor line on disagreement.
- On session start: read the cursor, verify against markers, announce "resuming at <page> × <role>", continue.
- Do not re-run completed agent checks on resume — unless the app version changed since the cursor's recorded version, in which case re-run agent rows for pages not yet human-validated.

---

## Recording findings

Each failure becomes a row in `00-inventory.md`:

```
| BUG-<PAGE>-<N> | bug | <page> [<role>] | <one-line summary> | open | P<N> | {{DATE}}-<slug> | — | — |
```

Severity guide:
- **P0** — a role cannot complete its goal (broken flow, blocked page)
- **P1** — mechanical failure on a primary page (console errors, broken breakpoint) or heavy judgment friction
- **P2** — degrades but does not block (awkward flow, unclear copy, minor visual drift)
- **P3** — polish

---

## Output artifacts

- `index.md` — run context, scope (pages × roles), session log
- `checklist.md` — per-page × per-role checklist + cursor (the resume state)
- `findings.md` — filtered view linking to `00-inventory.md`
- `evidence/` — per-check agent evidence: snapshots, console/network dumps, screenshots, Lighthouse reports

---

## Tips

- **Guard the boundary.** The pressure to "just have the human check everything" defeats the design; re-classify any human row a tool could verify reliably.
- **Agent first, always.** Human attention is the scarce resource — a page that fails mechanically wastes it.
- **Quote the human.** Paraphrased judgment calls lose the signal; record notes verbatim.
- **Finish the pair.** A half-marked page × role breaks the cursor; complete or revert before ending a session.
